+ * zest-gc: swap-slot-free hook, called from mm/swapfile.c swap_range_free()
+ * when [offset, offset+nr) are released. Clears the L2P/rmap entries and
+ * decrements the owning zones' valid_blocks so GC accounting stays exact
+ * (otherwise freed-but-not-overwritten blocks would be counted as valid and
+ * GC would needlessly relocate dead data). Runs under swap_info_struct::lock
+ * (atomic context): the implementation takes only zi->map_lock (a spinlock)
+ * and never sleeps. The lock is BH-safe because BIO completions may call back
+ * into swap-slot release from softirq context. Guarded by
+ * zest_should_intercept() at the call site.
